  <section class="cs-spacing">
    <div class="container" style="padding-top: 60px; padding-bottom: 60px;">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-10 offset-lg-1">
          <article style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#ddd;">
            <div class="lead" style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:32px;color:#bbb;">
              In the first 90 days of SEO, month one is diagnosis and foundations (technical audit, keyword mapping, tracking, quick fixes), month two is on-page and local work (page improvements, Google Business Profile, internal links, schema), and month three is content and authority building. By day 90 you should see leading indicators — more pages indexed, rising impressions, and first rankings for specific long-tail and local searches. Consistent leads and revenue from organic search usually take longer, often three to six months or more, depending on competition and your site's starting point.
            </div>
            <p style="font-size:13px;color:#999;margin-bottom:32px;">Published 2026-09-27 by Apex Marketings &middot; SEO</p>
            <style>article a {color:rgb(20,120,190);text-decoration:underline;} article h2 {margin-top:48px;} article h3 {margin-top:32px;}</style>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Why SEO takes time</h2>
              <p>Search engines need to crawl your changes, re-evaluate your pages, and see evidence over time that your site deserves to rank. Competitors are not standing still either. That is why an honest SEO partner talks about leading indicators first and revenue later, and why anyone promising "page one in two weeks" deserves suspicion.</p>
              <p>The good news is that the first 90 days are when the foundations are laid, and weak foundations are the reason many SEO campaigns stall.</p>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Month 1: diagnose and fix the foundations</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Tracking</strong> — Google Analytics 4 and Search Console set up correctly, with enquiries, calls and WhatsApp clicks tracked as conversions.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Technical audit</strong> — indexing, crawl errors, site speed, mobile usability, duplicate pages, redirects and structured data.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Keyword and competitor research</strong> — what your customers actually search, which terms have buying intent, and who ranks today.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Keyword mapping</strong> — one primary topic per page, so pages stop competing with each other.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Quick wins</strong> — fixing broken pages, improving titles and meta descriptions on pages already getting impressions.</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Month 2: on-page improvements and local SEO</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Service and category pages</strong> rewritten to answer buyer questions clearly, with strong calls to action.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Internal linking</strong> so important pages receive links from related content.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Schema markup</strong> for your business, services, FAQs and articles.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Google Business Profile</strong> — categories, services, photos, posts and a review process for real customers (see our <a href="../google-business-profile-optimization-guide/">GBP optimisation guide</a>).</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Citations</strong> — consistent name, address and phone across reputable directories.</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Month 3: content and authority</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>New content</strong> targeting questions buyers ask before they purchase — comparisons, costs, how-to guides.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Digital PR and links</strong> from relevant, reputable sites: partners, suppliers, industry associations, local media.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Conversion improvements</strong> on pages that now get traffic, so visitors become enquiries.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Review of month-one data</strong> to double down on what is moving.</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What results are realistic by day 90?</h2>
              <div class="table-responsive" style="margin:30px 0;overflow-x:auto;"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:560px;color:#ddd;"><caption style="caption-side:bottom;padding-top:10px;font-size:14px;color:#999;">Typical SEO indicators across the first 90 days. Timing varies with competition and starting point.</caption><thead><tr style="border-bottom:2px solid #e6ad02;"><th style="padding:14px 10px;color:#fff;text-align:left;">Timeframe</th><th style="padding:14px 10px;color:#fff;text-align:left;">What you can usually expect to see</th><th style="padding:14px 10px;color:#fff;text-align:left;">What is usually still ahead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Days 1–30</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Tracking live, technical issues fixed, baseline report</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Ranking changes are small</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Days 31–60</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">More pages indexed, impressions starting to rise, first long-tail movement</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Competitive head terms</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Days 61–90</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Rankings for specific long-tail and local searches, more map-pack visibility, first organic enquiries for some sites</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Consistent lead flow and revenue at scale</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
              <p>For a real example with verified numbers, read our case study on <a href="../zero-to-page-one-gcc-2-month-b2b-seo-playbook/">taking a B2B exporter from zero to page one in the GCC in two months</a>. It also shows the honest caveat: clicks and leads lag behind rankings.</p>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">KPIs to track each month</h2>
              <div class="table-responsive" style="margin:30px 0;overflow-x:auto;"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:560px;color:#ddd;"><caption style="caption-side:bottom;padding-top:10px;font-size:14px;color:#999;">SEO metrics worth reporting monthly.</caption><thead><tr style="border-bottom:2px solid #e6ad02;"><th style="padding:14px 10px;color:#fff;text-align:left;">KPI</th><th style="padding:14px 10px;color:#fff;text-align:left;">Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Indexed pages and crawl errors</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Pages that are not indexed cannot rank</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Impressions and average position (Search Console)</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">The earliest sign that Google is testing your pages</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Rankings for mapped keywords</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Progress on the terms that matter to revenue</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Organic sessions and engaged sessions</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Real visitors, not just rankings</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Enquiries, calls and WhatsApp clicks from organic</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">The number that pays for SEO</td></tr><tr style="border-bottom:1px solid #333;"><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;color:#fff;font-weight:600;min-width:120px;">Google Business Profile actions</td><td style="padding:12px 10px;vertical-align:top;">Calls, direction requests and website clicks from Maps</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Red flags in the first 90 days</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Guaranteed rankings or guaranteed numbers of leads.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">No access to your own Google Analytics, Search Console or Business Profile.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Reports full of vanity metrics with no link to enquiries.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">Large numbers of cheap backlinks from unrelated sites.</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;">No written plan of what will be done each month.</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What you need to provide</h2>
              <p>Access to your website, analytics and Business Profile; one person who can approve changes; honest information about which services and customers are most profitable; and help collecting reviews from real customers. SEO moves faster when the business is involved.</p>
              <p>Apex Marketings <a href="../../services/seo-services/">SEO retainers</a> start from USD 800 (about PKR 2.2 lakh) per month, with a written 90-day plan and monthly reporting — see full <a href="../../pricing/">pricing</a>.</p>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4 mt-5">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How long does SEO take to show results?</h3><p>Leading indicators such as indexing, impressions and long-tail rankings often appear within one to three months. Consistent leads and revenue from organic search usually take three to six months or longer, depending on competition, the site's history and how much work is done.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">What happens in the first month of SEO?</h3><p>The first month usually covers tracking setup, a technical audit, keyword and competitor research, keyword mapping to pages, and quick fixes such as broken pages and weak titles on pages already receiving impressions.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Can SEO guarantee first-page rankings?</h3><p>No. No agency controls Google's algorithm, so guaranteed rankings are a red flag. A good agency commits to the work it will do and the metrics it will report, not to positions it cannot control.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">What KPIs should an SEO report include?</h3><p>Useful SEO reports include indexed pages, Search Console impressions and positions, rankings for mapped keywords, organic sessions, organic enquiries and calls, and Google Business Profile actions for local businesses.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How much does SEO cost with Apex Marketings?</h3><p>Apex Marketings SEO retainers start from USD 800 per month (about PKR 2.2 lakh), and one-off SEO audits are also available. The final quote depends on the size of the site, competition and the markets you target.</p>
